@page "/"

<PageTitle>Athenaeum — Library API</PageTitle>

<section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">ASP.NET Core · .NET 10 · clean architecture</p>
        <h1>A library API<br />that answers back.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
            Books, categories, members and loans behind a CQRS pipeline — plus a
            Claude-powered chat that runs through the very same handlers your
            controllers call.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="chat">Open the chat</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="account">Sign in</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="stack">
            <span class="book book-1"></span>
            <span class="book book-2"></span>
            <span class="book book-3"></span>
            <span class="book book-4"></span>
            <span class="book book-5"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="orb"></div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="cards">
    <article class="card">
        <span class="card-glyph">🧭</span>
        <h2>One pipeline</h2>
        <p>
            Controller or component, every request lands on
            <code>IMediator</code> → handler → repository. The chat page sends
            <code>AskClaudeQuery</code> in-process, skipping a pointless HTTP hop
            to our own API.
        </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
        <span class="card-glyph">🛡️</span>
        <h2>One cookie</h2>
        <p>
            The Blazor circuit is authenticated by the same ASP.NET Identity
            cookie <code>/api/Auth/login</code> issues, so
            <code>[Authorize]</code> means the same thing in both worlds.
        </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
        <span class="card-glyph">⚡</span>
        <h2>Live over WebSocket</h2>
        <p>
            Interactive pages run on a Blazor Server circuit — a persistent
            WebSocket back to the host. No client bundle, no token plumbing,
            no second deploy.
        </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
        <span class="card-glyph">🗄️</span>
        <h2>Chat touches no database</h2>
        <p>
            Conversations live in <code>IMemoryCache</code> for thirty minutes.
            The library tables are never read or written by the chat slice.
        </p>
    </article>
</section>
